'''TimelineRail''' draws a vertical timeline: a date column, a rail with dots, and the events. It uses only wikitext and [[mw:Extension:TemplateStyles|TemplateStyles]] (no script is needed) and follows the reader's light or dark theme. It is a family of six templates: {{tl|TimelineRail}}, {{tl|TimelineRail/item}}, {{tl|TimelineRail/event}}, {{tl|TimelineRail/parallel}}, {{tl|TimelineRail/gap}} and {{tl|TimelineRail/section}}, with the stylesheet in <code>Template:TimelineRail/styles.css</code>.
Needs <code>#if</code> (ParserFunctions). Do not leave blank lines between items or events: wikitext turns them into stray paragraphs inside the list.

== Simple: one event per dot ==
<pre>
{{TimelineRail
|{{TimelineRail/item |date=1612 |title=The Go academy |text=The Tokugawa shogunate patronises the game.}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=c. 1651 |title=Huang Longshi |text=Born. |image=Huang Longshi.jpg |caption=Huang Longshi}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=March 2016 |title=AlphaGo defeats Lee Sedol}}
}}
</pre>

== Several events on one dot ==
<pre>
{{TimelineRail
|{{TimelineRail/item |date=2006 |events=
{{TimelineRail/event |title=Crazy Stone |text=Monte Carlo tree search arrives in Go.}}
{{TimelineRail/event |title=UCT |text=The UCT algorithm is published.}}
}}
}}
</pre>

== Collapsible items (default) ==
Every item that has content is collapsible. Clicking its dot or date hides its content, and the title moves to the date row after a pipe: <code>1846 | The Ear-Reddening Game</code>. This uses MediaWiki's built-in collapsible feature (the same as navboxes), so the template adds no script of its own, but the toggle needs the reader's browser to run it; without JavaScript the item simply stays open.
* <code>collapsed=yes</code>: start collapsed.
* <code>collapsible=no</code>: not collapsible.
* <code>summary=</code>: the text after the pipe for an item with several events (a one-event item uses its <code>title</code>).
* <code>id=</code>: only needed if two items on the same page share the same date and title; the id is otherwise made from the date and title.
An optional user script, <code>Timeline-collapse-all.js</code>, adds a double-click on any dot to collapse or expand the whole timeline.
<pre>
{{TimelineRail
|{{TimelineRail/item |date=1846 |title=The Ear-Reddening Game |text=Shusaku's move 127 stuns Gennan Inseki.}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=2006 |collapsed=yes |summary=Crazy Stone and UCT |events=
{{TimelineRail/event |title=Crazy Stone |text=Monte Carlo tree search arrives in Go.}}
{{TimelineRail/event |title=UCT |text=The UCT algorithm is published.}}
}}
}}
</pre>

== Sections (nestable) ==
<code>TimelineRail/section</code> goes among the items of a <code>TimelineRail</code> (or of another section). It shows a red dot and a <code>title</code>; its content, which is a list of items and more sections, is indented, and clicking the red dot collapses all of it. Sections nest to any depth. Add <code>collapsed=yes</code> to start collapsed; <code>id=</code> only if two sections on a page share a title.
On a wide window the title goes in the date column, to the left of the rail, like a date; on a narrow one it follows the dot. A section can also carry text and an image beside the dot, which stay visible when it is collapsed: <code>text=</code>, <code>image=</code> (a file name), <code>imagesize=</code>, <code>imagealt=</code> and <code>caption=</code>, the same as for an item with one event.
<pre>
{{TimelineRail
|{{TimelineRail/section |title=Early history
|{{TimelineRail/item |date=1612 |title=The Go academy}}
{{TimelineRail/section |title=Edo period
|{{TimelineRail/item |date=1846 |title=The Ear-Reddening Game}}
}}
}}
}}
</pre>
With text beside the dot:
<pre>
{{TimelineRail
|{{TimelineRail/section |title=Edo period |text=Four centuries of state-sponsored Go.
|{{TimelineRail/item |date=1612 |title=The Go academy}}
}}
}}
</pre>

== Nested timelines ==
Give an item a <code>sub</code> parameter holding more <code>TimelineRail/item</code>s. They appear indented under that item, with their own rail, and can nest further. Do not indent the wikitext lines with spaces (that makes a preformatted block); the indentation is in the rendering.
<pre>
{{TimelineRail
|{{TimelineRail/item |date=1990s |title=Neural networks meet Go |sub=
{{TimelineRail/item |date=1994 |title=NeuroGo}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=1996 |title=Golem}}
}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=2016 |title=AlphaGo}}
}}
</pre>

== Parallel timelines (several timelines on one row) ==
Wrap timelines in <code>TimelineRail/parallel</code> and give each a <code>title</code>. They share the row and wrap onto the next one when there is no horizontal space. Each keeps its own dates and rail; nothing lines up across them. Inside a row the timelines always use the narrow layout (date above the events).
<pre>
{{TimelineRail/parallel
|{{TimelineRail |title=Players
|{{TimelineRail/item |date=1846 |title=The Ear-Reddening Game}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=November 2019 |title=Lee Sedol retires}}
}}
{{TimelineRail |title=Programs
|{{TimelineRail/item |date=1968 |title=First Go program}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=2006 |events=
{{TimelineRail/event |title=Crazy Stone}}
{{TimelineRail/event |title=UCT}}
}}
}}
}}
</pre>

== Parallel and grouped timelines (dots aligned) ==
Add <code>grouped=yes</code>. At 640 px and wider the n-th item of every timeline then sits on the same row, so dots line up horizontally. To skip a row in one timeline, put <code>{{TimelineRail/gap}}</code> in its place. Rules: every timeline needs a <code>title</code>; at most 20 items (including gaps) per timeline; do not end a timeline with gaps. The columns share the width and do not wrap; below 640 px the timelines fall back to the independent, wrapping layout.
<pre>
{{TimelineRail/parallel |grouped=yes
|{{TimelineRail |title=Players
|{{TimelineRail/item |date=1846 |title=The Ear-Reddening Game}}
{{TimelineRail/gap}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=March 2016 |title=Lee Sedol wins game 4}}
}}
{{TimelineRail |title=Programs
|{{TimelineRail/gap}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=1968 |title=First Go program}}
{{TimelineRail/item |date=March 2016 |title=AlphaGo wins the match}}
}}
}}
</pre>

== Parameters ==
; TimelineRail/parallel: <code>1</code> timelines; <code>grouped</code> (set to anything to align dots).
; TimelineRail: <code>1</code> items; <code>title</code> (optional heading; use it inside a row).
; TimelineRail/item: <code>date</code>; either <code>title</code>, <code>text</code>, <code>image</code>, <code>imagesize</code>, <code>imagealt</code>, <code>caption</code> (one event) or <code>events</code> (several <code>TimelineRail/event</code>); optional <code>sub</code> (nested <code>TimelineRail/item</code>s); optional <code>collapsed</code>, <code>collapsible=no</code>, <code>summary</code>, <code>id</code>, <code>last</code> (set to anything on the final item: the line ends at its dot).
; TimelineRail/event: same fields as the one-event shorthand.
; TimelineRail/gap: no parameters.
; TimelineRail/section: <code>title</code>, <code>1</code> (items and sections), <code>collapsed</code>, <code>id</code>; optional <code>text</code>, <code>image</code>, <code>imagesize</code>, <code>imagealt</code>, <code>caption</code> (shown beside the dot).
